              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 6,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "PCgAn",
                  "name": "Title",
                  "fill": "$color/text",
                  "content": "P · Filter — narrow or hide by Category, Group, Account and Person in List, Month and Insights",
                  "fontFamily": "$font/family",
                  "fontSize": 30,
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "gwwPI",
                  "name": "Desc",
                  "fill": "$color/text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": 1300,
                  "content": "docs/prd/expense-filter.md. A Filter button in the toolbar opens one sheet: four rows (Category · Group · Account · Person), each pushing a checklist of every entity, alphabetical, its empty value last (Uncategorized · No group · Unassigned · No one). Several values per dimension combine with OR, dimensions with AND, and the plan filter with AND. Ticks apply live. While a filter is on, SPENDING shows the filtered total with “of Rp <whole>” under it, and the split describes the filtered set. Expenses and Insights keep separate filters; paging ‹ › resets the Expenses one, the Insights one survives chip and pay period changes. The Plan lens and Search ignore it. An active filter is marked by the lit Filter button with a badge (active dimensions) and a glass pill above the tab bar, stacked over the plan pill when both are on (mark B, owner's choice; A and C stay on page 05). Built 10 Oct 2026; on device the badge is the system's red toolbar badge, and on Expenses the button shares Monthly Start Date's glass capsule. One sample: payday 31, today Thu 6 Aug 2026. Since §4.9 (P12–P17), every checklist row cycles Off → Only → Hidden on each tap, the empty values too: within a row an expense passes when it matches any Only value (if there is one) and carries no Hidden value, and a hidden Person hides every expense that includes them. Hidden wears nosign in red and dims the name; summaries say “not” (“Not Cicilan, Kos”, “Category · not Cicilan, Kos”, “Fadil, not Tarisa”). The Plan row has no Hidden state. Built 10 Oct 2026.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "fontFamily": "$font/family",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
