              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "S0Prv1",
                  "name": "Title",
                  "fill": "$color/text",
                  "content": "Q · Assign an expense to an Envelope — by hand, from the envelope, or many at once",
                  "fontFamily": "$font/family",
                  "fontSize": 30,
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "iZEGq",
                  "name": "Desc",
                  "fill": "$color/text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": 1300,
                  "content": "docs/prd/envelope-assignment.md. An Envelope counts expenses by Category; a trip cannot be described that way. The expense editor gains an Envelope row under Category: By category (the default, naming where the Category lands), No envelope (Outside plan), or any active Envelope of that cycle's plan. An assigned expense counts in its envelope only, never in the one that claims its Category. An Envelope may now claim no Category at all. Shortcuts: a ＋ on each Envelope row in the Plan lens adds an expense already assigned, and Select in the List lens moves many expenses at once. One sample: the -seedPlanData normal plan plus a Travelling envelope (Rp 2.000.000, no Categories) holding Nasi Padang Bandung 85.000, Bensin ke Bandung 150.000 and Hotel Bandung 450.000 → Rp 1.315.000 left; Kado ultah Tarisa (Makan 250.000) is No envelope. Hidup stays at Rp 226.900 left. Built 13 Oct 2026 as schema V4 (Expense.envelope + isOutsideEnvelopes). On device, Select mode also hides search, and since the tab bar is gone while selecting, switching tabs cannot happen until Done; By category reads “Choose a category first” before a Category is picked. Flow R (13 Oct 2026) replaced the Select button with a long-press menu on every row and made the envelope's ＋ a menu with Move expenses here….",
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "fontFamily": "$font/family",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
