                  "fill": "$color/text",
                  "content": "U · Paid early moves money between plans",
                  "fontFamily": "$font/family",
                  "fontSize": 30,
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "D3oi7",
                  "name": "Desc",
                  "fill": "$color/text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": 1300,
                  "content": "docs/prd/envelope-assignment.md §4.10.10, ADR-0009 (amended). Built 14 Oct 2026, no schema change. Flow S counted the ticket in November's Travelling bar but left both plans' Sisa alone, so the money was set aside twice. A paid-early expense now moves its amount from the plan of its own cycle (October: \"→ Paid early for November −Rp 1.200.000\", Sisa and the SISA headline fall) to the plan of its envelope's cycle (November: \"→ Paid early in October +Rp 1.200.000\", Sisa rises, capped at the envelope's planned amount). Total cost stays Σ planned; drift is unchanged (owner override: the envelope's whole overspend stays in Over plan so far); transfer lines and Group shares count the envelope net, and the transfer row's second line names the credit, wrapping to two lines rather than truncating the envelope's name. Sample: §7.1 — Tiket KAI ke Jakarta Rp 1.200.000 on 14 Oct into November's Travelling Rp 2.000.000 on BCA.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "fontFamily": "$font/family",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
