                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "D85eWI",
                  "name": "Desc",
                  "fill": "$color/text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": 1300,
                  "content": "docs/prd/envelope-assignment.md §4.11, decision log §8.3. Built 16 Oct 2026, no schema change. On device a paid-early row's note wrapped over five lines in a column ~90pt wide, beside a tag cut to “Travel ke… · Nov”: ExpenseMetaLine put the tag and the note side by side, the tag had layout priority and up to 150pt. Now every tag kind (Fixed, Envelope, Paid early) sits on its own line above the Category, hugging its text up to the width of the text column; only the name truncates, never “· ‹Mon›”. The note gets the whole column back; untagged rows are unchanged; Envelope detail stays untagged. VoiceOver reads the tag first. V1–V3 use the §7.1 sample (-seedPlanData paid-early, payday 25) plus a Kopi logged by hand. Options B, C and D are kept on 05 as not chosen. Every older flow on this page now draws its tags the same way.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "fontFamily": "$font/family",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
