                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "cQNXl",
                  "name": "Desc",
                  "fill": "$color/text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": 1300,
                  "content": "docs/prd/bank-logos.md, ADR-0012. Built 17 Oct 2026, schema V6 (Account.brandID). An Account can wear a bank logo from a catalog the developer keeps in CloudKit's public database (record type BankLogo) and changes at any time; the app refetches the whole catalog on launch and foreground, at most every 10 minutes, and ships a snapshot for before the first fetch. The owner's name for the Account never changes. Logos are a Banks section in the Icon pane, drawn in a white circle the size of the icon circle, never tinted. Plan chips, section headers and Insights' proportion rows keep a bare glyph (building.columns). A withdrawn logo falls back to that glyph. Expense rows show the Account under the amount (X9). Images are the placeholder snapshot: initials in the brand colour. On device: -brandAccounts bca,mandiri,jago and -bankCatalog fetched|withdrawn-mandiri|empty.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "fontFamily": "$font/family",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
