                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "dEF7T",
                      "name": "Note",
                      "fill": "$color/text-secondary",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "§5.2, decision 7. BCA, Mandiri and Jago wear logos, but a Plan chip's glyph is 10pt and a section header's 14pt: too small for a logo. They show building.columns instead of the card glyph, so a bank still reads as a bank. BNI, CC Danamon and Cash have no logo and keep their own symbol. M2's sample, otherwise unchanged.",
                      "fontFamily": "$font/family",
                      "fontSize": 14,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
