                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "w5f9P",
                  "name": "Desc",
                  "fill": "$color/text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": 1300,
                  "content": "docs/prd/bank-logos.md §5.5 (amended), decisions 23–31. Built 18 Oct 2026, the day after flow Y. The owner wanted the banks clearly visible in the expense list and picked option A of eight directions (the rest stay on 05 · Proposals). ExpenseRowMark leads every row: the Account's 42pt mark (logo in a white circle with 12% padding, its own symbol, or the bank glyph when the logo is withdrawn) with the category as an 18pt solid badge ringed 1pt in the card colour, hanging 4pt past the corner; the row's spacing is 14. The Account's name stays under the amount, without a mark. An Unassigned expense leads with its 42pt category icon. Insights › one Account (or a drill-in narrowed to one) keeps the category-first row via the expenseRowAccountsLead environment value. Rows are ~62pt with a one-line meta.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.45,
                  "fontFamily": "$font/family",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
