                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "l6CM8o",
                  "name": "Desc",
                  "fill": "$color/text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": 1300,
                  "content": "docs/prd/bank-logos.md §5.6 (amended), decisions 32–46. Built 18 Oct 2026. The owner picked option C of flow AA's six directions (the rest stay on 05 · Proposals), the Transfer checklist in C's style and option A's chip. Sorted by Account, each group opens with PlanAccountHeader: a 60×28 AccountPlate (the catalog logo cropped to its wordmark on white; a logo-less Account its symbol on its wash; Unassigned grey), the name and count, the group's total and its state — nothing in yet · Rp X to go · all in BNI · all paid — and the rows drop their Account chip and Funded \"in BNI\". In every other order PlanAccountChip keeps the grey chip with a small white wordmark plate and the name, dropping the name only when the chip line cannot fit. The Transfer checklist (TransferRow · bank) leads with the plate, names the Account without \"ke\", puts the amount on the name's line and reads count · due days · notes beneath. Same October sample as flow AA's options; BCA has its own checklist line, as the app draws it.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.45,
                  "fontFamily": "$font/family",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
