                      "content": "Sorted by Account only. Each group opens with the bank: a 60×28 plate (the cropped wordmark on white; Cash its symbol on its wash), the Account's name and count, and on the right the group's total — the sum of its items — and its state: nothing in yet · Rp X to go (the ◯ items) · all in BNI (accent) · all paid (green). Envelopes and Auto items follow the same rule. Rows inside drop the Account chip and the Funded \"in BNI\": the header says both. Unassigned (no Account) closes the list with a grey plate and only \"to go\" / \"all paid\".",
