                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Amount, Due day, Group, Status and Name order (and the Funded filter, which forces Amount). A bank Account's chip stays the grey chip: the building.columns glyph becomes a small white plate with the cropped wordmark, and the Account's name always follows it — owner's call, so two Accounts at one bank never look alike — unless the chip line cannot fit on one line, when the name drops and the plate stays (Cicilan Rumah BNI, Cicil ke Kartu Kredit, Netflix). Cash keeps its banknote symbol. A Funded row keeps its trailing \"in BNI\" here.",
