                      "fill": "$color/text-secondary",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Today's Plan lens with the same plan. Every bank chip is the same building.columns glyph plus the Account's name in 12pt grey, so BNI, BCA and Mandiri read alike and the name does all the work; Cash keeps its own symbol. Sorted by Account (X7), the section headers use the same 14pt glyph. The Transfer checklist (E3) is text only — \"ke BNI\". The bank is never the first thing the eye lands on: the check, the item name and the amount are.",
