                      "content": "Smallest change. Plan: a bank Account's chip becomes a white pill with its cropped wordmark (10pt tall — BCA ≈ 31pt wide, Superbank ≈ 61pt) instead of glyph + name; Cash keeps today's grey symbol chip, and the chip line gets shorter (Netflix's Auto now fits). Transfer checklist: \"ke\" + the same pill. Everything else as shipped, so Plan sorted by Account can reuse the pill in its headers. Cost: the white pill is the brightest thing in the chip line and outshouts the category; Danamon's lettering is only ~4pt tall; two Accounts at one bank (BCA Gaji / BCA Tabungan) would need the name after the logo. Pattern: payment-method chips at Tokopedia / Shopee checkout.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.45,
                      "fontFamily": "$font/family",
                      "fontSize": 14,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
