                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "QBlgA",
                      "name": "Note",
                      "fill": "$color/text-secondary",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Matches the expense list's chosen Z·A, so both lenses read the same. Plan: the Account's logo leads each row in a 42pt white circle (Cash: its banknote circle); the DoneCheck shrinks to a 16pt badge on the circle's corner (Todo ring, Done tick, Funded half, Auto bolt) and the circle becomes the check's tap target; the Account chip goes away, \"in BNI\" stays while Funded. Transfer checklist: the same circle leads, the sent tick is its badge. Cost: the plan's main job — ticking things off — loses its 26pt check, so \"what is still to do\" is harder to scan; one mark now carries two meanings (where the money is + its state); a Funded half-circle at 16pt is barely readable. Pattern: Copilot Money / Revolut scheduled payments.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.45,
                      "fontFamily": "$font/family",
                      "fontSize": 14,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
