                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "cuwsj",
                      "name": "Note",
                      "fill": "$color/text-secondary",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Only Plan sorted by Account changes (M · Account, X7). Each group opens with the bank: a 60×28 white wordmark plate, the Account name and item count, and on the right what that bank must cover this cycle plus its state (\"all in BNI\", \"Rp 1.500.000 to go\", \"nothing in yet\"). Rows inside drop the Account chip — the header says it once. Transfer checklist: the same plate leads each line, named by Account with its item count (\"2 items · Due 12, 20\"), so a line and its group read as one. Answers \"what must BCA cover, and is it there yet?\" — the payday question. Cost: in Amount / Due / Group order nothing changes (banks stay glyphs there, or take A's pill); one header per Account. Pattern: bank statements, Wise balances, YNAB's account groups.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.45,
                      "fontFamily": "$font/family",
                      "fontSize": 14,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
