                      "name": "Note",
                      "fill": "$color/text-secondary",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "A sideways rail of bank tiles above the plan, one per Account: wordmark plate, name, what it must cover, a funded bar and \"all in BNI\" / \"0 of 2 in\". Tapping a tile filters the plan to that Account (it reuses flow P's Account filter, ringed in accent; tap again or \"Show all 10 items\" to clear). Transfer checklist: a 36pt logo circle after the check. Rows stay as shipped. The banks get a permanent, glanceable home at the top of the Plan. Cost: ~130pt of height before the first plan item; three tiles fit, the other four scroll; it repeats what C's headers say, but without re-sorting. Superbank's 6:1 wordmark is near-unreadable in the 36pt circle. Pattern: Jago Pockets, Jenius, Revolut's account carousel.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.45,
                      "fontFamily": "$font/family",
                      "fontSize": 14,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
