                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "Q4stc5",
                      "name": "Note",
                      "fill": "$color/text-secondary",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "The Account's logo becomes the row's 42pt leading mark (white circle, wordmark at ~74% of the width, so letters are ~7pt tall vs ~4pt today). The category shrinks to a 20pt badge on its corner, ringed in the card colour, and keeps the bold title. The trailing side is just the amount and the Account name — no second mark. Cash and other brandless Accounts lead with their own symbol circle. Pattern: Copilot Money / Revolut, where the payee or source leads and the category is a badge.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.45,
                      "fontFamily": "$font/family",
                      "fontSize": 14,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
