                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "FEyvH",
                      "name": "Note",
                      "fill": "$color/text-secondary",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Inside a day card the rows sit under their Account: a white wordmark chip (logo cropped to its wordmark, 24pt tall — the biggest the logo gets in any option) and the Account name; the Account's day total shows only when it has two or more rows, so it never repeats a row's amount. Rows lose their account label and keep today's category icon, so both identities stay. Groups follow each Account's first expense; rows inside keep time order. Answers \"what did BCA pay for today?\" at a glance; the cost is a header per Account, which makes a day of single-row Accounts long. Pattern: bank statements, Wise's per-balance activity.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.45,
                      "fontFamily": "$font/family",
                      "fontSize": 14,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
