                      "id": "Evdn7",
                      "name": "Note",
                      "fill": "$color/text-secondary",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "The day card splits into one small card per expense, like passes in Wallet. Each card's leading edge is a 4pt stripe in the Account's brand colour (the catalog's tintHex; Cash uses its own tint), and its top line is a wordmark chip with the Account name — the plan tag moves to the right end of that line. Below, today's category icon, title, meta and a slightly larger amount. The bank is the first thing on every card and the stripe makes runs of one bank visible while scrolling. Cost: ~25% taller per expense, so fewer rows per screen, and a long list feels busier than today's grouped cards.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.45,
                      "fontFamily": "$font/family",
                      "fontSize": 14,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
